Title: Lake District runner airlifted to safety during 55-mile race
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [], 'Description': [{'Description': 'An ultramarathon runner was airlifted to safety after he collapsed from the heat during a 55-mile (88.5km) mountain race, rescuers have said.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 111}}, {'Description': 'Patterdale Mountain Rescue Team (PMRT) were called to Grisedale Valley, in the Lake District, at about 16:00 BST on Saturday after the runner became pale, vomited and lost consciousness.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 165}}, {'Description': 'North West Ambulance Service contacted mountain rescue as well as the coastguard, which sent a helicopter to winch the man to safety before taking him to the King George playing field in Patterdale.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 188}}, {'Description': 'PMRT said the runner was then "checked over by a team doctor at Patterdale Base and transferred to hospital for further checks".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 110}}, {'Description': 'PMRT said the rescue lasted two and a half hours and involved 11 team members, as well as the coastguard.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 89}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Two white Land Rovers with orange and green liveries parked next to a road. Two people in orange coats are starting to walk away form the vehicles, with a lake and trees behind them'}]}
